      "body": "Note: The feature I'm kind of talking about here would be kind of a combination of taskbar and workspaces.\r\n\r\nGiven the following workspaces and windows:\r\n![image](https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/assets/38593283/cebaab2a-e8d6-4ad6-8a97-73741f62e768)\r\n\r\nThis is how my workspaces and taskbar show up in my waybar:\r\n- Workspaces\r\n  - 1\r\n  - 2\r\n  - 3\r\n- Taskbar\r\n  - Window A\r\n  - Window B\r\n  - Window M\r\n  - Window N\r\n  - Window Y\r\n  - Window Z\r\n\r\nWhich makes it difficult to see how I have things organized.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice to have a unified module that presents that information in a somewhat hierarchical nature, either like this:\r\n\r\n| |\r\n| --- |\r\n|**1** |\r\n| Window A |\r\n| Window B |\r\n|**2** |\r\n| Window M |\r\n| Window N |\r\n|**3** |\r\n| Window Y |\r\n| Window Z |\r\n\r\nOr\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/assets/38593283/5bc28616-382d-4d66-95e1-728343c71971)\r\n",
