      "body": "## Environment\nI'm using **Arch Linux**, **Hyprland** and **Waybar**\n<img width=\"1283\" height=\"621\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7789336b-a4d4-4a88-885b-2254207b2bc0\" />\n\n## Problem description\nWhen I'm using Firefox/Chromium and I open an application with icons in the title, the waybar automatically increase the height, as shown in the image below: \n<img width=\"1918\" height=\"195\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a11240a-b5e6-4677-a789-321c9fde3ba5\" />\n\nbut, the normal height is: \n\n<img width=\"1917\" height=\"83\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c887b74-e258-4e81-8057-a289cc12eaf4\" />\n\n## My configuration\n\n### Title configuration\n```\n  \"hyprland/window\": {\n    \"format\": \"<span font='14px'><span color='#97b4f2'>󰊠</span> {title}</span>\",\n    \"tooltip\": false\n  },\n```\n\n### Global style\n```\n* {\n  font-family: GeistMono Nerd Font;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  min-height: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n```",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Alexays/Waybar/issues/4785/reactions",
